WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.759
All right, let's get into audience questions
for the week.

00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:06.149
Just days left until the election.

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:09.250
Many election related questions, including
first and foremost, David, I've heard you

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.170
criticize Donald Trump's response to the virus.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:13.559
And I agree with you.

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:14.910
It has been terrible.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:20.060
But if Joe Biden becomes president in January,
what should he do then?

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.780
That Donald Trump has not done so.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.110
Two part question, first of all, is the vast
majority of the things that should have been

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.690
done should have been done previously.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:35.820
And this includes establishing contact tracing
early on, building testing capacity early

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:42.670
on the way that South Korea did, telling the
truth early on about the seriousness of the

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.670
virus.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:47.469
A lot of these things in other words, most
people now understand the seriousness of the

00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:48.469
virus.

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:51.620
There's less to do on that front, although
you still have a lot of Trump's followers

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.620
who don't believe it.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.269
It would be great to have to have a president
who tells the truth.

00:00:55.269 --> 00:01:02.170
But there is no question that the time to
do things was 20/20, not 20 or 21, which is

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.650
when Joe Biden will actually get to do something.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:11.900
Now, by January 21st, hopefully we would start
to be on the other side of Spike number three,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.290
which is building right now.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:19.870
Hopefully by January 21st, there will already
be some people vaccinated and more people

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.180
getting vaccinated every day.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:27.550
So the things that Joe Biden will have to
sort of think about or contend with will be,

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:34.250
number one, restoring our public health officials
who are actually infectious disease specialists

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:37.030
to positions where they are speaking to the
country.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:42.330
Dr. Anthony Foushee was removed from that
position by Trump and blocked from doing interviews

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.010
and so on and so forth.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:50.110
He put in neuro radiologist Scott Atlas, who
wants herd immunity and questions, masks and

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.140
whatever else.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:56.230
So we've got to change who is publicly speaking
to the country from the standpoint of public

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.360
health.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.280
Stop lying about the virus.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.170
Constantly get a stimulus bill done.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.940
If indeed we need one January 21st.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:10.899
And that's something that a President Biden
would have to look at, evaluate whether the

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:15.050
request for mask mandates should be made.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:22.379
Remember, the consensus constitutionally seems
to be that a president cannot federally mandate

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:23.830
everybody wear a mask.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.290
There would be two ways to do it.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:32.030
One is a president would say to all 50 governors,
hey, guys and gals, please do mask mandates.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.400
If we all do this for six weeks.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.329
We will dramatically reduce the spread.

00:02:38.329 --> 00:02:42.609
It would be up to governors to do it or work
with Congress so that through the Commerce

00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:48.270
Clause court, Congress can regulate commerce
in such a way that would allow some kind of

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.270
mass mandate.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.469
But a president unilaterally doing it doesn't
appear as though they can do it.

00:02:52.469 --> 00:02:53.750
This is the way we'd have to be done.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:59.079
Biden's going to have to evaluate the situation
if and when he gets sworn in and go from there.

00:02:59.079 --> 00:03:03.859
You know, things like a national contact tracing
system.

00:03:03.859 --> 00:03:07.409
The unfortunate reality, it would be great
to do it.

00:03:07.409 --> 00:03:13.799
The unfortunate reality is that contact tracing,
once you have overwhelming communities spread

00:03:13.799 --> 00:03:19.409
where even relatively rural parts of the country
have a huge number of cases.

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:24.879
Contact tracing becomes less important at
a at a systemic public health level.

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:26.060
It should still be done.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:31.370
But again, the time to do it was in February
and March.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:39.069
Increased transparency on the numbers because
now many people don't trust the numbers actually

00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:46.650
work with other countries, as opposed to saying,
we're blocking China, we're blocking Europe.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:51.200
Everybody that Americans get blocked from
going places actually start to work with other

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:57.200
countries on a coordinated response, planning
for what things will start to look like as

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.389
we can hopefully at some point next year,
begin to loosen travel guidelines, so on and

00:04:02.389 --> 00:04:08.059
so forth, assure us of the safety of the vaccine
in a trustworthy way.

00:04:08.059 --> 00:04:14.680
As you all know, without being anti vax, anybody
who has followed the lies of Trump would be

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:21.090
skeptical about saying on Trump's say so that
a vaccine is safe.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.030
So there are lots of things to be done.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:29.590
But we also have to recognize that we talk
about climate change, irreversible damage.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:33.590
And when someone else comes in, they have
to start trying to clean up a situation that

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.510
was worsened, not under their watch.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:40.670
A lot of the things on coronavirus had to
be done when Australia did them, when New

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:46.490
Zealand did them, when South Korea did them,
when Taiwan did the Bangladesh, etc. by the

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.500
time Joe Biden is in office.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.960
Those things aren't the things anymore.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:56.940
And it will be about figuring out going forward
how to restore trustworthiness and a sense

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.990
of professionalism to the White House in its
coronavirus response.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.840
And it's going to be an uphill battle, there's
no doubt about it.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.810
But every day, every day we wait is another
day.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.400
Trump's federal government pushes us in the
wrong direction

